IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-periods`
IMPORT `era-notice`
IMPORT `era-unfair-dismissal`
IMPORT `era-redundancy`
IMPORT `era-goal`

-- Independent tests for the ERA 1996 encoding. Every expected value was
-- written in independent-expectations.md from the Act alone, before the
-- encoding was read. Scenario ids (N1, Q3, T9, B4, P27, ...) refer to that file.
-- A failing assertion is a finding: expected values are not to be changed to
-- match the code.

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, s IS A DATE, pay IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Employee`
mkEmp dob s pay MEANS `Employee` OF dob, s, pay

GIVEN s IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Employee`
startedOn s MEANS mkEmp (Date 15 6 1980) s 500

GIVEN n IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
employerNotice n e MEANS `Termination` OF `terminated by the employer`, JUST n, e, FALSE

GIVEN e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
employerSummary e MEANS `Termination` OF `terminated by the employer`, NOTHING, e, FALSE

GIVEN e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
constructive e MEANS `Termination` OF `terminated by the employee, entitled to do so without notice by the employer's conduct`, NOTHING, e, FALSE

GIVEN e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
constructiveDuringNotice e MEANS `Termination` OF `terminated by the employee, entitled to do so without notice by the employer's conduct`, NOTHING, e, TRUE

GIVEN n IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
resigns n e MEANS `Termination` OF `terminated by the employee otherwise`, JUST n, e, FALSE

GIVEN e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
limitedTerm e MEANS `Termination` OF `a limited-term contract ended by the limiting event without renewal`, NOTHING, e, FALSE

-- Unfair dismissal facts: s 64(2)?, no qualifying period?, early conciliation, reason, s 122(4) payments.
GIVEN s64 IS A BOOLEAN, noq IS A BOOLEAN, ec IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`, r IS A `Reason for dismissal`, rp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
mkUD s64 noq ec r rp MEANS `Unfair dismissal facts` OF s64, noq, NOTHING, ec, FALSE, TRUE, r, 0, rp

udPlain MEANS mkUD FALSE FALSE NOTHING `an ordinary reason` 0

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
ecAB a b MEANS JUST (`Early conciliation` OF a, b)

GIVEN r IS A `Reason for dismissal`, rp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
udReason r rp MEANS mkUD FALSE FALSE NOTHING r rp

-- Redundancy facts: reason (MAYBE), s 140, s 141, paid, written claim, tribunal reference, EC, just and equitable.
GIVEN red IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, cond IS A BOOLEAN, refd IS A BOOLEAN, paid IS A MAYBE DATE, wr IS A MAYBE DATE, ref IS A MAYBE DATE, ec IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`, je IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Redundancy facts`
mkRF red cond refd paid wr ref ec je MEANS `Redundancy facts` OF red, cond, refd, FALSE, paid, wr, ref, NOTHING, ec, je

-- A plain redundancy: presumed (s 163(2)), written claim on the day given.
GIVEN wr IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Redundancy facts`
claimOn wr MEANS mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST wr) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE

rfPlain MEANS claimOn (Date 1 2 2026)

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
erWeeks emp d MEANS `the notice in weeks the employer must give` emp `on` d

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
eeWeeks emp d MEANS `the notice in weeks the employee must give` emp `on` d

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
erExpiry emp d MEANS `the day the employer's statutory notice given on` d `to` emp `would expire`

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
qualifies emp t u MEANS `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` emp `for` t `with` u

GIVEN t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A DATE
lastDay t u MEANS `the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
award emp t u MEANS `the basic award for` emp `and` t `with` u

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`, r IS A `Redundancy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
entitled emp t r MEANS `is entitled to a redundancy payment` emp `for` t `with` r

GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A NUMBER
amount emp t MEANS `the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` emp `and` t

GIVEN e IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
endedOn e MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 1 2000) e

§ `Goal 1 — minimum notice (s 86)`

-- N1-N2: one month beginning 1 Mar 2026 ends 31 Mar.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS Date 7 4 2026
-- N3-N4: one month beginning 31 Jan 2026 ends 28 Feb.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS Date 7 3 2026
-- N5-N6: the two-year edge.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS Date 6 1 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- N7: 2 years 11 months.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 2 2023)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 2 2023)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- N8-N10: the twelve-year edge and the cap.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2014)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2014)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS Date 17 3 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2014)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT eeWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2014)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2014)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 25 3 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 1 1 2000)) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2000)) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS Date 24 8 2026
-- N11-N14: started 29 Feb 2024.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS Date 6 3 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS Date 14 3 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 27 3 2024) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 28 3 2024) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (Date 28 3 2024) EQUALS Date 4 4 2024
-- N15: expiry crossing 29 Feb 2028.
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 1 1 2027)) (Date 25 2 2028) EQUALS Date 3 3 2028
-- N16-N17: the seventh year.
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 15 5 2019)) (Date 13 5 2026) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 15 5 2019)) (Date 13 5 2026) EQUALS Date 24 6 2026
#ASSERT erWeeks (startedOn (Date 15 5 2019)) (Date 14 5 2026) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT erExpiry (startedOn (Date 15 5 2019)) (Date 14 5 2026) EQUALS Date 2 7 2026

§ `Goal 2a — qualifying period (s 108, s 97(2)/(4))`

udS64 MEANS mkUD TRUE FALSE NOTHING `an ordinary reason` 0
udNoQual MEANS mkUD FALSE TRUE NOTHING `an ordinary reason` 0

-- Q1-Q2
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2025)) udPlain
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 1 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 30 12 2025)) udPlain)
-- Q3-Q4
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 28 2 2026)) udPlain
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 29 2 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 27 2 2026)) udPlain)
-- Q5
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 31 8 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 1 8 2026) (Date 30 8 2026)) udPlain
-- Q6-Q8: s 97(2)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 10 1 2024)) (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) udPlain
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 10 1 2024)) (employerSummary (Date 1 1 2026)) udPlain)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 10 1 2024)) (employerNotice (Date 4 1 2026) (Date 7 1 2026)) udPlain
-- Q9-Q10: s 97(4)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 8 1 2024)) (constructive (Date 2 1 2026)) udPlain
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 8 1 2024)) (constructiveDuringNotice (Date 2 1 2026)) udPlain)
-- Q11-Q14: s 108(2)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (employerNotice (Date 24 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026)) udS64
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 3 2026)) (employerSummary (Date 30 3 2026)) udS64)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (employerNotice (Date 21 2 2026) (Date 28 2 2026)) udS64
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 31 1 2026)) (employerSummary (Date 27 2 2026)) udS64)
-- Q15-Q18: s 108(3)-(5) (one input flag in this encoding)
#ASSERT qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 1 2026)) (employerNotice (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026)) udNoQual
-- Q19
#ASSERT NOT (qualifies (startedOn (Date 1 1 2026)) (employerNotice (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026)) udPlain)

§ `Goal 2b — last day to present a complaint (s 111(2)(a), s 207B)`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
udEC a b MEANS mkUD FALSE FALSE (ecAB a b) `an ordinary reason` 0

-- T1-T8 without early conciliation
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) udPlain EQUALS Date 14 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 30 11 2025)) udPlain EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 29 11 2025)) udPlain EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 28 11 2025)) udPlain EQUALS Date 27 2 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 30 11 2027)) udPlain EQUALS Date 29 2 2028
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 29 11 2027)) udPlain EQUALS Date 28 2 2028
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 31 3 2026)) udPlain EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 31 12 2025)) udPlain EQUALS Date 30 3 2026
-- T9-T18 with Day A / Day B, EDT 15 Jan 2026 (limit 14 Apr 2026)
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 2 2026)) EQUALS Date 28 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 10 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 5 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 13 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 21 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 13 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 5 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 5 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 15 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 14 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 14 4 2026) (Date 14 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 14 5 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 16 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 11 6 2026
-- T19-T20 month ends
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 30 11 2025)) (udEC (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 27 2 2026)) EQUALS Date 27 3 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 1 11 2025)) (udEC (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026)) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- T21: s 97(2) does not move the s 111 date
#ASSERT lastDay (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) udPlain EQUALS Date 1 4 2026

§ `Goal 2c — basic award (ss 119-122, 227)`

b1Emp MEANS mkEmp (Date 15 6 1980) (Date 1 1 2016) 500
b1Term MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2025)

-- B1-B2
#ASSERT award b1Emp b1Term udPlain EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 15 6 1980) (Date 1 1 2016) 1000) b1Term udPlain EQUALS 9012
-- B3-B6: birthdays on, and one day after, the first day of the latest year
b3Term MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 3 1984) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term udPlain EQUALS 2600
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 2 3 1984) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term udPlain EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 3 2003) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term udPlain EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 2 3 2003) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term udPlain EQUALS 1200
-- B7-B8: twenty-year limit
b7Term MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 9 2025) (Date 31 12 2025)
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 1 2000) 900) b7Term udPlain EQUALS 22530
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1980) (Date 1 1 2000) 600) b7Term udPlain EQUALS 13500
-- B9: under 22 throughout
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 9 2003) (Date 1 9 2020) 300) (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 31 8 2025)) udPlain EQUALS 750
-- B10: a part year does not count
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2020) 500) (employerNotice (Date 1 5 2025) (Date 30 6 2025)) udPlain EQUALS 2500
-- B11: s 97(2) adds the twelfth year
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1970) (Date 3 3 2014) 500) (employerSummary (Date 28 2 2026)) udPlain EQUALS 9000
-- B12-B14: s 120 minimums
b12Emp MEANS mkEmp (Date 1 1 1980) (Date 1 1 2025) 500
b12Term MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 30 6 2025)
#ASSERT award b12Emp b12Term (udReason `a reason listed in s 120(1)` 0) EQUALS 9157
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 1 2000) 900) b7Term (udReason `a reason listed in s 120(1)` 0) EQUALS 22530
#ASSERT award b12Emp b12Term (udReason `a blacklist reason under s 104F` 0) EQUALS 5000
-- B15-B16: s 121
#ASSERT award b1Emp b1Term (udReason `redundancy, within s 121` 0) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 15 6 1980) (Date 1 1 2016) 800) b1Term (udReason `redundancy, within s 121` 0) EQUALS 1502
-- B17-B19: s 122(4)
#ASSERT award b1Emp b1Term (udReason `an ordinary reason` 6000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT award b1Emp b1Term (udReason `an ordinary reason` 2000) EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT award b1Emp b1Term (udReason `an ordinary reason` 8000) EQUALS 0
-- B20: s 120 minimum is before the s 122 reduction
#ASSERT award b12Emp b12Term (udReason `a reason listed in s 120(1)` 1000) EQUALS 8157

§ `Goal 3 — redundancy payment (ss 135-164)`

-- P1-P5 amounts
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp b1Term rfPlain
#ASSERT amount b1Emp b1Term EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 15 6 1980) (Date 1 1 2016) 1000) b1Term EQUALS 9012
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 1 2000) 900) b7Term EQUALS 22530
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 3 1984) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term EQUALS 2600
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 2 3 1984) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 3 2003) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 2 3 2003) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term EQUALS 1200
-- P6-P7: s 163(2)
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp b1Term (mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp b1Term (mkRF (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE))
-- P8: resignation is not a dismissal
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp (resigns (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2025)) rfPlain)
-- P9-P10: constructive dismissal and limited-term expiry are dismissals
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp (constructive (Date 31 12 2025)) rfPlain
#ASSERT amount b1Emp (constructive (Date 31 12 2025)) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp (limitedTerm (Date 31 12 2025)) rfPlain
#ASSERT amount b1Emp (limitedTerm (Date 31 12 2025)) EQUALS 6000
-- P11: no s 145(5) for an employee's termination
#ASSERT NOT (entitled (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 8 1 2024) 500) (constructive (Date 2 1 2026)) rfPlain)
-- P12-P13: s 145(5)
#ASSERT entitled (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 10 1 2024) 500) (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) rfPlain
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 10 1 2024) 500) (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT NOT (entitled (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 10 1 2024) 500) (employerSummary (Date 1 1 2026)) rfPlain)
-- P14
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1970) (Date 3 3 2014) 500) (employerSummary (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS 9000
-- P15-P16: ss 140, 141
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp b1Term (mkRF NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp b1Term (mkRF NOTHING FALSE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE))
-- P17-P18: s 155
#ASSERT NOT (entitled (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2024) 500) (employerNotice (Date 1 12 2025) (Date 30 12 2025)) rfPlain)
#ASSERT entitled (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2024) 500) b1Term rfPlain
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2024) 500) b1Term EQUALS 1000

-- s 164: relevant date 15 Mar 2026
rd15Mar MEANS employerNotice (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026)
GIVEN wr IS A DATE, je IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Redundancy facts`
writtenJE wr je MEANS mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST wr) NOTHING NOTHING je

-- P19-P22
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (writtenJE (Date 14 9 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (writtenJE (Date 15 9 2026) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (writtenJE (Date 15 9 2026) FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (writtenJE (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE))
-- P23-P26: month-end six months
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 8 2026)) (writtenJE (Date 28 2 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 8 2026)) (writtenJE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE))
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 30 8 2027)) (writtenJE (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 29 8 2027)) (writtenJE (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE))
#ASSERT `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` (employerNotice (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 8 2026)) EQUALS Date 28 2 2027
-- P27-P29: s 164(5) and s 207B
ecSep MEANS ecAB (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 10 9 2026)
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 10 2026)) ecSep FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (Date 11 10 2026)) ecSep FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (entitled b1Emp rd15Mar (mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 10 2026)) NOTHING ecSep FALSE))
-- P30: s 145(5) does not move the s 164 period
p30Emp MEANS mkEmp (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 10 1 2024) 500
#ASSERT `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) EQUALS Date 1 7 2026
#ASSERT NOT (entitled p30Emp (employerSummary (Date 2 1 2026)) (writtenJE (Date 5 7 2026) FALSE))
-- P31: agreed and paid
#ASSERT entitled b1Emp b1Term (mkRF NOTHING FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE)

§ `Top-level goal`

-- B1/P1 through the default export: complaint presented on 1 Feb 2026.
goalUD MEANS `Unfair dismissal facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 1 2 2026), NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, `an ordinary reason`, 0, 0
goalCase MEANS `Dismissal case` OF b1Emp, b1Term, goalUD, rfPlain
goalPos MEANS `the dismissal position for` goalCase
#ASSERT goalPos's `weeks of notice the employer had to give` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT goalPos's `weeks of notice the employee had to give` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT goalPos's `effective date of termination` EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
#ASSERT goalPos's `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`
#ASSERT goalPos's `last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint` EQUALS Date 30 3 2026
#ASSERT goalPos's `basic award` EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT goalPos's `entitled to a redundancy payment`
#ASSERT goalPos's `redundancy payment` EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT goalPos's `last day of the s 164(1) period` EQUALS Date 30 6 2026

-- Complaint presented after the s 111 limit, no late allowance: no basic award.
lateUD MEANS `Unfair dismissal facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 31 3 2026), NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, `an ordinary reason`, 0, 0
lateCase MEANS `Dismissal case` OF b1Emp, b1Term, lateUD, rfPlain
latePos MEANS `the dismissal position for` lateCase
#ASSERT latePos's `basic award` EQUALS 0

§ `Probes added after reading the encoding (expected values from the Act)`

-- T22-T23: Day A before the effective date of termination.
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 4 2026
#ASSERT lastDay (endedOn (Date 15 1 2026)) (udEC (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026)) EQUALS Date 14 4 2026
-- B21-B22, P32: a year of employment reckoned back across 29 Feb cannot begin before employment began.
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 3 1983) (Date 1 3 2024) 400) (employerNotice (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 28 2 2025)) udPlain EQUALS 600
#ASSERT award (mkEmp (Date 1 3 1979) (Date 1 3 2020) 400) b3Term udPlain EQUALS 3600
#ASSERT amount (mkEmp (Date 1 3 1983) (Date 1 3 2024) 400) (employerNotice (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 28 2 2025)) EQUALS 600
